  "description": {
    "la": "Didascalicon de studio legendi, in sex libris: quid discendum, quo ordine et quomodo, de artibus et de Scripturis.",
    "en-US": "Hugh’s guide to study in six books: what is to be learned, in what order and how, from the arts of philosophy (Books I-III) to the reading of Scripture, with the famous counsel to “learn everything; you will see afterwards that nothing is superfluous”. The seventh book of the Migne text, On the Three Days, is a separate book. Latin only, from the Migne text (Patrologia Latina 176, 1854), a machine-corrected OCR.",
    "pt-BR": "O guia de estudo de Hugo em seis livros: o que se deve aprender, em que ordem e como, das artes da filosofia (livros I a III) à leitura da Escritura. O sétimo livro do texto de Migne, Sobre os três dias, é um livro à parte."
  },
  "composed": "c. 1127",
  "languages": [
    "la"
  ],
  "work": "hugh/didascalicon",
  "editions": {
    "la": {
      "editor": "J.-P. Migne (Patrologia Latina 176)",
      "year": 1854
    }
  },
  "sources": [
    {
      "language": "la",
      "url": "https://mlat.uzh.ch/php_modules/download.php?type=file-xml&idno=HuDeSVi.EruDid",
      "edition": "Migne, Patrologia Latina 176 (Paris 1854); TEI XML of the Corpus Corporum (University of Zurich), text HuDeSVi.EruDid, from the machine-corrected OCR of the Open Greek and Latin project.",
      "description": "The complete PL text with its chapter divisions. PL page breaks and column numbers are dropped, and the PL tables of chapters (which repeat the chapter headings) are not imported. The OCR carries a few residual slips.",
      "tier": "A",
      "tierEvidence": "Migne’s Patrologia Latina (1854–1855) prints the medieval text; public domain everywhere."
    }
  ],
